msgid "Solana wallet"
msgstr "Πορτοφόλι Solana"

#. Error in the Solana payout wallet's connect sheet of the desktop apps (macOS, Windows, Linux) when the ur.io wallet bridge page returns extension_not_found: the chosen wallet's browser extension is not in this browser. The argument is the wallet product name (Phantom or Solflare). The sheet also takes a typed address, which works with any wallet, so the line points at its Enter address manually control, named in that control's own words (enter_address_manually). Signing in has no manual entry and keeps bittensor_error_extension_not_found.
msgctxt "solana_wallet_error_extension_not_found"
msgid "The {} extension was not found in this browser. Install it and try again, or choose “Enter address manually” to paste your wallet address."
msgstr "Η επέκταση {} δεν βρέθηκε σε αυτό το πρόγραμμα περιήγησης. Εγκαταστήστε την και δοκιμάστε ξανά ή επιλέξτε «Χειροκίνητη εισαγωγή διεύθυνσης» για να επικολλήσετε τη διεύθυνση του πορτοφολιού σας."

#. Solana wallet error in the desktop apps (macOS, Windows, Linux) when the ur.io wallet bridge page returns session_not_found: the browser no longer has the wallet connection made in the connect step (another browser or a private window, or its site data was cleared), so nothing was signed. Starting again reconnects the wallet (Phantom or Solflare).
msgctxt "solana_wallet_error_session_not_found"
msgid "The wallet connection wasn't found in this browser. Start again to reconnect your wallet."
msgstr "Η σύνδεση του πορτοφολιού δεν βρέθηκε σε αυτό το πρόγραμμα περιήγησης. Ξεκινήστε ξανά για να συνδέσετε ξανά το πορτοφόλι σας."

#. Used in Main/Account/Wallets/ConnectWalletSheet/ConnectWalletSheetView.swift.
msgctxt "solflare"
msgid "Solflare"
msgstr "Solflare"

#. Something went wrong error message
msgctxt "something_went_wrong"
msgid "Something went wrong."
msgstr "Κάτι πήγε στραβά."

#. Snackbar shown when the account lookup for a password reset fails. Used in Main/Account/Profile/ProfileView.swift.
msgctxt "something_went_wrong_finding_your_account"
msgid "Something went wrong finding your account"
msgstr "Κάτι πήγε στραβά κατά την εύρεση του λογαριασμού σας"

#. Used in Main/Account/Settings/UpdateReferralNetworkSheet/UpdateReferralNetworkSheetViewModel.swift.
msgctxt "something_went_wrong_please_try_again_later"
msgid "Something went wrong. Please try again later."
msgstr "Κάτι πήγε στραβά. Παρακαλώ δοκιμάστε ξανά αργότερα."

#. Call to action
msgctxt "sorry_to_see_you_go"
msgid "We're sorry to see you go!"
msgstr "Λυπούμαστε που φεύγετε!"

#. A label displaying the number of split rules. The argument is the count of split rules.
msgctxt "split_rule_count"
msgid "{} split rule"
msgid_plural "{} split rules"
msgstr[0] "{} κανόνας διαχωρισμού"
msgstr[1] "{} κανόνες διαχωρισμού"

#. A description of the functionality of the split rule editor.
msgctxt "split_rule_description"
msgid "Selected hosts are routed locally and bypass the tunnel."
msgstr "Οι επιλεγμένοι hosts δρομολογούνται τοπικά και παρακάμπτουν το τούνελ."

#. Split rules: validation error for a host entry that is not a valid host name.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_bad_name"
msgid "Enter a host name like example.com."
msgstr "Εισαγάγετε ένα όνομα κεντρικού υπολογιστή όπως example.com."

#. Split rules: validation error for an entry that looks like an IP range but is not a valid CIDR.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_bad_range"
msgid "Enter an IP range like 10.0.0.0/8."
msgstr "Εισαγάγετε ένα εύρος IP όπως 10.0.0.0/8."

#. Split rules: validation error for a wildcard entry with nothing after the asterisk.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_bad_wildcard"
msgid "A wildcard needs a name after it, like *.example.com."
msgstr "Ο χαρακτήρας μπαλαντέρ χρειάζεται ένα όνομα μετά από αυτόν, όπως *.example.com."

#. Split rules: validation error when a broader entry already in the rule covers the typed one. {rule} is that broader entry, for example *.example.com or 10.0.0.0/8.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_covered"
msgid "Already covered by {} in this rule."
msgstr "Καλύπτεται ήδη από το {} σε αυτόν τον κανόνα."

#. Split rules: validation error when the typed entry is already in the rule.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_duplicate"
msgid "Already in this rule."
msgstr "Υπάρχει ήδη σε αυτόν τον κανόνα."

#. Split rules: validation error for a host name with non-ASCII characters; the rule wants the punycode form.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_not_ascii"
msgid "Use the ASCII form of the name."
msgstr "Χρησιμοποιήστε τη μορφή ASCII του ονόματος."

#. Split rules: placeholder in the host input listing the accepted forms (a host name, a wildcard, a CIDR range).
msgctxt "split_rule_host_placeholder"
msgid "example.com, *.example.com, 10.0.0.0/8"
msgstr "example.com, *.example.com, 10.0.0.0/8"

#. Split rule editor: description of the Route locally mode.
msgctxt "split_rule_mode_excluded_description"
msgid "Selected hosts bypass the tunnel."
msgstr "Οι επιλεγμένοι hosts παρακάμπτουν τη σήραγγα."

#. Split rule editor: description of the Route through VPN mode (the default). A pin is the Keep on one provider mode.
msgctxt "split_rule_mode_included_description"
msgid "The default: selected hosts use the tunnel with no pin."
msgstr "Η προεπιλογή: οι επιλεγμένοι hosts χρησιμοποιούν τη σήραγγα χωρίς καρφίτσωμα."

#. Split rule editor: description of the Keep on one provider mode.
msgctxt "split_rule_mode_pinned_description"
msgid "Selected hosts hold their provider longer instead of being moved at the first sign of trouble, so the site changes IP addresses less often mid-session."
msgstr "Οι επιλεγμένοι hosts κρατούν τον πάροχό τους περισσότερο αντί να μετακινούνται με το πρώτο σημάδι προβλήματος, ώστε ο ιστότοπος να αλλάζει διεύθυνση IP λιγότερο συχνά κατά τη συνεδρία."

#. Split rule editor: title of the mode that keeps the selected hosts on the same VPN provider longer.
msgctxt "split_rule_mode_pinned_title"
msgid "Keep on one provider"
msgstr "Διατήρηση σε έναν πάροχο"

#. Split rules preset: Google Meet call media, from the address ranges Google publishes for routing it outside a VPN. Keep the product name Google Meet unchanged.
msgctxt "split_rule_preset_google_meet_calls"
msgid "Google Meet calls"
msgstr "Κλήσεις Google Meet"

#. Split rules preset: Microsoft Teams call media, from the address ranges Microsoft publishes for routing it outside a VPN. Keep the product name Microsoft Teams unchanged.
msgctxt "split_rule_preset_microsoft_teams_calls"
msgid "Microsoft Teams calls"
msgstr "Κλήσεις Microsoft Teams"

#. transfer stats and split rules
msgctxt "split_rules"
msgid "Split rules"
msgstr "Κανόνες διαχωρισμού"

#. A description of the content of the "Activity" section of the split rules view.
msgctxt "split_rules_activity_hint"
msgid "Routing activity appears here while connected."
msgstr "Η δραστηριότητα δρομολόγησης εμφανίζεται εδώ όταν είστε συνδεδεμένοι."

#. Split rules screen: note under the disabled Add a rule button before the app has connected once and loaded the saved rules.
msgctxt "split_rules_connect_to_load"
msgid "Connect once to load the rules you already have."
msgstr "Συνδεθείτε μία φορά για να φορτωθούν οι κανόνες που έχετε ήδη."

#. A description of how to route traffic locally.
msgctxt "split_rules_hint"
msgid "Tap traffic below to route it locally, bypassing the tunnel."
msgstr "Πατήστε την κίνηση παρακάτω για να δρομολογηθεί τοπικά, παρακάμπτοντας το τούνελ."

#. Split rules on android, which has a host input above the traffic list: how to add to the rule. The apple/linux screens without the input keep split_rules_hint.
msgctxt "split_rules_host_hint"
msgid "Add a host above, or tap traffic below to route it locally, bypassing the tunnel."
msgstr "Προσθέστε έναν κεντρικό υπολογιστή παραπάνω ή πατήστε την κίνηση παρακάτω για να δρομολογηθεί τοπικά, παρακάμπτοντας το τούνελ."

#. Split rules screen: hint shown while there are no rules yet. Routing locally sends traffic outside the VPN; holding to one provider keeps a site on the same VPN exit.
msgctxt "split_rules_host_hint_modes"
msgid "Add a host above, or tap traffic below to route it locally or hold it to one provider."
msgstr "Προσθέστε έναν host παραπάνω ή πατήστε την κίνηση παρακάτω για να τη δρομολογήσετε τοπικά ή να την κρατήσετε σε έναν πάροχο."

#. transfer stats and split rules
msgctxt "split_rules_info_note"
msgid "Exclusions apply to the whole co-associated network cluster, so related traffic is caught together."
msgstr "Οι εξαιρέσεις ισχύουν για ολόκληρη τη συσχετισμένη ομάδα δικτύων, ώστε η σχετική κίνηση να καλύπτεται μαζί."

#. Split rules screen: note that a rule matches every host in the same network cluster (related hosts of one site or service), whatever the rule's mode.
msgctxt "split_rules_info_note_modes"
msgid "Rules apply to the whole co-associated network cluster, so related traffic is caught together."
msgstr "Οι κανόνες ισχύουν για ολόκληρο το συσχετισμένο σύμπλεγμα δικτύων, ώστε η σχετική κίνηση να καλύπτεται μαζί."

#. Split rules screen on macOS 15 and later: the rules match sites and addresses, and an app is kept off the VPN by adding it in the Apps section below (the section is titled with the "Apps" string, so use the same word as that title). Notes that local network addresses already bypass the VPN. Keep Mac and VPN unchanged.
msgctxt "split_rules_match_sites_and_apps_macos"
msgid "Split rules match sites and addresses. To keep an app off the VPN on this Mac, add it under Apps. Local network addresses already bypass the VPN."
msgstr "Οι κανόνες διαχωρισμού ισχύουν για ιστότοπους και διευθύνσεις. Για να κρατήσετε μια εφαρμογή εκτός VPN σε αυτό το Mac, προσθέστε την στις Εφαρμογές. Οι διευθύνσεις του τοπικού δικτύου παρακάμπτουν ήδη το VPN."

#. Split rules screen (iOS/macOS): why the rules match sites and addresses rather than apps. Apple's per-app VPN (NEAppRule) is available only on devices an organization manages (MDM). Points to host rules and presets, and notes that local network addresses already bypass the VPN. Keep Apple, VPN and MDM unchanged.
msgctxt "split_rules_match_sites_not_apps"
msgid "Split rules match sites and addresses, not apps: Apple allows per-app VPN only on devices managed by an organization (MDM). To keep an app off the VPN, route the sites it uses locally, or start from a preset. Local network addresses already bypass the VPN."
msgstr "Οι κανόνες διαχωρισμού ισχύουν για ιστότοπους και διευθύνσεις, όχι για εφαρμογές: η Apple επιτρέπει VPN ανά εφαρμογή μόνο σε συσκευές που διαχειρίζεται κάποιος οργανισμός (MDM). Για να κρατήσετε μια εφαρμογή εκτός VPN, δρομολογήστε τοπικά τους ιστότοπους που χρησιμοποιεί ή ξεκινήστε από μια προεπιλογή. Οι διευθύνσεις του τοπικού δικτύου παρακάμπτουν ήδη το VPN."

#. Split rules screen: header of the preset menu. Each preset holds the address ranges its service publishes for routing that service's traffic outside a VPN.
msgctxt "split_rules_preset_ranges_header"
msgid "Ranges each service publishes for use outside a VPN"
msgstr "Εύρη που δημοσιεύει κάθε υπηρεσία για χρήση εκτός VPN"

#. Split rules screen: the menu that starts a route-locally rule from a preset, the address ranges a service publishes for use outside a VPN.
msgctxt "split_rules_start_from_preset"
msgid "Start from a preset"
msgstr "Έναρξη από προεπιλογή"

#. Split rules screen on macOS, Apps section: the split tunnel extension or its proxy configuration could not be installed or started, so the listed apps still use the VPN. The Retry button follows; macOS asks the user to allow URnetwork's proxy configuration the first time. Keep VPN and macOS unchanged.
msgctxt "split_tunnel_apps_not_bypassing"
msgid "These apps can't bypass the VPN right now. Retry, and allow the proxy configuration if macOS asks."
msgstr "Αυτές οι εφαρμογές δεν μπορούν να παρακάμψουν το VPN αυτή τη στιγμή. Προσπαθήστε ξανά και επιτρέψτε τη διαμόρφωση διακομιστή μεσολάβησης, αν το ζητήσει το macOS."

#. Split rules screen on macOS, Apps section: the split tunnel system extension waits for the user's one-time approval in System Settings (General > Login Items & Extensions > Network Extensions). Use the name macOS gives System Settings in the language. Keep URnetwork Split Tunnel (the extension's name) and VPN unchanged.
msgctxt "split_tunnel_extension_needs_approval"
msgid "To keep these apps off the VPN, allow the URnetwork Split Tunnel extension in System Settings."
msgstr "Για να κρατήσετε αυτές τις εφαρμογές εκτός VPN, επιτρέψτε την επέκταση URnetwork Split Tunnel στις Ρυθμίσεις συστήματος."

#. macOS error when adding a sign-in method could not open the browser for the provider's sign-in page.
msgctxt "sso_browser_open_failed"
msgid "Could not open the browser. Please try again."
msgstr "Δεν ήταν δυνατό το άνοιγμα του προγράμματος περιήγησης. Δοκιμάστε ξανά."

#. Error when a browser sign-in (Google or Apple through the browser) took too long and expired.
msgctxt "sso_sign_in_timed_out"
msgid "Sign-in timed out. Please try again."
msgstr "Η σύνδεση έληξε. Δοκιμάστε ξανά."

#. Guest mode overlay
msgctxt "start_earning_join"
msgid "To start earning, join the network"
msgstr "Για να ξεκινήσετε να κερδίζετε, γίνετε μέλος του δικτύου"

#. Primary button of the plan picker (onboarding and upgrade): starts the paid plan's free trial. Replaces 'Join the movement'.
msgctxt "start_free_trial"
msgid "Start free trial"
msgstr "Έναρξη δωρεάν δοκιμής"

#. Confirmation button that keeps the user on the seedphrase screen after the warning.
msgctxt "stay"
msgid "Stay"
msgstr "Παραμονή"

#. Used as a headline in the Initial Auth carousel.
msgctxt "stay_completely_private_and_anonymous"
msgid "Stay completely private and anonymous"
msgstr "Μείνετε εντελώς ιδιωτικοί και ανώνυμοι"

#. Settings
msgctxt "stay_in_touch"
msgid "Stay in touch"
msgstr "Μείνετε σε επαφή"

#. Button under the selected provider in the Provider Locations sheet. Reconnects to that one provider (the exit), so the connection keeps its IP address.
msgctxt "stay_on_this_exit"
msgid "Stay on this exit"
msgstr "Παραμονή σε αυτή την έξοδο"

#. Muted line under the Stay on this exit button in the Provider Locations sheet: what staying on one provider does.
msgctxt "stay_on_this_exit_note"
msgid "Keeps this provider's IP address until it goes offline."
msgstr "Διατηρεί τη διεύθυνση IP αυτού του παρόχου μέχρι να αποσυνδεθεί."

#. Onboarding Carousel
msgctxt "stay_private"
msgid "Stay\ncompletely\nprivate and\nanonymous"
msgstr "Παραμείνετε\nεντελώς\nιδιωτικοί και\nανώνυμοι"

#. Onboarding Carousel
msgctxt "stay_private_description"
msgid "Stay completely private and anonymous with URnetwork"
msgstr "Παραμείνετε εντελώς ιδιωτικοί και ανώνυμοι με το URnetwork"

#. Muted line on the provider the connection already stays on (after Stay on this exit), in the Provider Locations sheet. Says how to leave it.
msgctxt "staying_on_this_exit"
msgid "Staying on this exit. If it goes offline, choose another location."
msgstr "Παραμένετε σε αυτή την έξοδο. Αν αποσυνδεθεί, επιλέξτε άλλη τοποθεσία."

#. Login initial
msgctxt "step_in"
msgid "Step into the internet as it should be."
msgstr "Μπείτε στο διαδίκτυο όπως θα έπρεπε να είναι."

#. Guidance for someone who has no code yet. Deliberately PLAIN TEXT with no link and no button: app store rules forbid steering a user to an external purchase, but nothing stops us saying where codes come from. Without this, the sheet asks for a code and gives no way to obtain one.
msgctxt "step_into_the_internet"
msgid "Step into the internet\nas it should be."
msgstr "Μπείτε στο διαδίκτυο\nόπως θα έπρεπε να είναι."

#. Call to action
msgctxt "step_one"
msgid "Step 1"
msgstr "Βήμα 1"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "step_two"
msgid "Step 2"
msgstr "Βήμα 2"

#. Points leaderboard: stat tile label and sort chip. Consecutive blocks with points.
msgctxt "streak"
msgid "Streak"
msgstr "Σερί"

#. Connect drawer: strong anonymization toggle — the inverse of allow direct (direct connections expose the real source IP to the provider).
msgctxt "strong_anonymization"
msgid "Strong Anonymization"
msgstr "Ισχυρή ανωνυμοποίηση"

#. Locations list: screen reader name of the icon on a location whose country has strong privacy laws.
msgctxt "strong_privacy_laws"
msgid "Strong privacy laws"
msgstr "Αυστηροί νόμοι για την ιδιωτικότητα"

#. Button on the plan picker for the monthly plan, which has no free trial.
msgctxt "subscribe"
msgid "Subscribe"
msgstr "Εγγραφή"

#. Snackbar error when the Stripe subscription management page (Manage subscription) could not be opened.
msgctxt "subscription_portal_open_failed"
msgid "Couldn't open the subscription portal. Please try again."
msgstr "Δεν ήταν δυνατό το άνοιγμα της πύλης συνδρομής. Δοκιμάστε ξανά."

#. The store purchase belongs to a different network than the one logged in — crediting must not go to the wrong account, so tell the user which way out exists. Apple: restore-purchases outcome (Shared/ViewModels/AppStoreSubscriptionManager.swift). Android: terminal `wrong_network` answer from the Play purchase report (google/PlanViewModel.kt); the purchase is still acknowledged so Play does not auto-refund it.
msgctxt "subscription_purchased_under_different_account"
msgid "Your subscription was purchased under a different account. Log in to that account to use it."
msgstr "Η συνδρομή σας αγοράστηκε με άλλον λογαριασμό. Συνδεθείτε σε εκείνον τον λογαριασμό για να τη χρησιμοποιήσετε."

#. Snackbar shown when the earnings multiplier is claimed successfully. Used in Main/Account/Settings/SettingsView.swift.
msgctxt "successfully_claimed_multiplier"
msgid "Successfully claimed multiplier!"
msgstr "Η αξίωση του πολλαπλασιαστή ολοκληρώθηκε με επιτυχία!"

#. A heading for a list of suggested remote DNS servers.
msgctxt "suggested_remote_dns_servers"
msgid "Suggested remote DNS servers"
msgstr "Προτεινόμενοι απομακρυσμένοι διακομιστές DNS"

#. A description of the suggested DNS servers.
msgctxt "suggested_remote_dns_servers_description"
msgid "Suggestions for the connected country are marked with its color. Turning one on adds it to the remote DNS servers."
msgstr "Οι προτάσεις για τη συνδεδεμένη χώρα επισημαίνονται με το χρώμα της. Αν ενεργοποιήσετε μία, προστίθεται στους απομακρυσμένους διακομιστές DNS."

#. Navigation: the Support tab, page or section, where users send feedback and contact the URnetwork support team. Customer support, not backing; use the word the language uses for a support team.
msgctxt "support"
msgid "Support"
msgstr "Υποστήριξη"

#. Upgrade subscription overlay
msgctxt "support_us"
msgid "Support us in building a new kind of network that gives instead of takes."
msgstr "Υποστηρίξτε μας στην οικοδόμηση ενός νέου τύπου δικτύου που δίνει αντί να παίρνει."

#. Display name for the paid plan. The WIRE value stays "supporter" (subscription_type / current_subscription.plan) because already-shipped app versions parse that string; only what the user reads changes.
msgctxt "supporter"
msgid "Pro"
msgstr "Pro"

#. Windows banner text when installing, starting or updating the VPN service failed.
msgctxt "svc_action_failed"
msgid "That didn't finish — the service is unchanged. Details are in the app log."
msgstr "Η ενέργεια δεν ολοκληρώθηκε — η υπηρεσία δεν άλλαξε. Λεπτομέρειες υπάρχουν στο αρχείο καταγραφής της εφαρμογής."

#. Settings: label of the VPN service row.
msgctxt "svc_service_label"
msgid "VPN service"
msgstr "Υπηρεσία VPN"

#. Windows banner button that installs the VPN service (Windows asks for administrator permission).
msgctxt "svc_setup_action"
msgid "Set up"
msgstr "Ρύθμιση"

#. Windows banner text under 'Set up the VPN service'.
msgctxt "svc_setup_message"
msgid "URnetwork uses a Windows service to carry traffic. One click — Windows will ask for administrator permission."
msgstr "Το URnetwork χρησιμοποιεί μια υπηρεσία των Windows για τη μεταφορά της κίνησης. Ένα κλικ — τα Windows θα ζητήσουν άδεια διαχειριστή."

#. Windows banner title when the URnetwork Windows service that carries traffic is not installed yet.
msgctxt "svc_setup_title"
msgid "Set up the VPN service"
msgstr "Ρύθμιση της υπηρεσίας VPN"

#. Windows banner button that starts the stopped VPN service.
msgctxt "svc_start_action"
msgid "Start"
msgstr "Έναρξη"

#. Windows banner text under 'Start the VPN service'.
msgctxt "svc_start_message"
msgid "The service is installed but not running."
msgstr "Η υπηρεσία είναι εγκατεστημένη αλλά δεν εκτελείται."

#. Windows banner title when the VPN service is installed but stopped.
msgctxt "svc_start_title"
msgid "Start the VPN service"
msgstr "Έναρξη της υπηρεσίας VPN"

#. Windows banner text after the user closed the administrator permission (UAC) prompt without approving.
msgctxt "svc_uac_declined"
msgid "Windows asked for permission and the prompt was closed. Click again whenever you're ready."
msgstr "Τα Windows ζήτησαν άδεια και το παράθυρο έκλεισε. Κάντε κλικ ξανά όταν είστε έτοιμοι."

#. Settings: button that uninstalls the VPN service.
msgctxt "svc_uninstall_action"
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr "Απεγκατάσταση"

#. Settings: confirmation text before uninstalling the VPN service.
msgctxt "svc_uninstall_confirm"
msgid "This stops the URnetwork service and removes its systemd unit. The app can't connect until it is set up again. You will be asked for administrator permission."
msgstr "Αυτό σταματά την υπηρεσία URnetwork και αφαιρεί τη μονάδα systemd της. Η εφαρμογή δεν μπορεί να συνδεθεί μέχρι να ρυθμιστεί ξανά. Θα σας ζητηθεί άδεια διαχειριστή."

#. Windows Settings: confirmation dialog before uninstalling the VPN service.
msgctxt "svc_uninstall_confirm_windows"
msgid "This stops the URnetwork service and removes it from Windows. The app can't connect until it is set up again. Windows will ask for administrator permission."
msgstr "Αυτό σταματά την υπηρεσία URnetwork και την αφαιρεί από τα Windows. Η εφαρμογή δεν μπορεί να συνδεθεί μέχρι να ρυθμιστεί ξανά. Τα Windows θα ζητήσουν άδεια διαχειριστή."

#. Settings: explanation under the uninstall service button.
msgctxt "svc_uninstall_note"
msgid "Remove the systemd service URnetwork uses to carry traffic."
msgstr "Αφαίρεση της υπηρεσίας systemd που χρησιμοποιεί το URnetwork για τη μεταφορά κίνησης."

#. Windows Settings > VPN service row: what the Uninstall button removes.
msgctxt "svc_uninstall_note_windows"
msgid "Remove the Windows service URnetwork uses to carry traffic."
msgstr "Αφαίρεση της υπηρεσίας Windows που χρησιμοποιεί το URnetwork για τη μεταφορά κίνησης."

#. Windows banner text under 'Update the VPN service'. The two version numbers follow it in parentheses.
msgctxt "svc_update_message"
msgid "The installed service is a different version than this app."
msgstr "Η εγκατεστημένη υπηρεσία έχει διαφορετική έκδοση από αυτήν την εφαρμογή."

#. Windows banner title when the installed VPN service is a different version than the app.
msgctxt "svc_update_title"
msgid "Update the VPN service"
msgstr "Ενημέρωση της υπηρεσίας VPN"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "switch_account"
msgid "Switch Account"
msgstr "Αλλαγή λογαριασμού"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "switch_account_details"
msgid "Do you want to disconnect from {} and switch accounts?"
msgstr "Θέλετε να αποσυνδεθείτε από το {} και να αλλάξετε λογαριασμούς;"

msgctxt "symbol_dash"
msgid "-"
msgstr "-"

#. An ellipsis character used to indicate ongoing processing.
msgctxt "symbol_ellipsis"
msgid "..."
msgstr "..."

msgctxt "symbol_empty"
